WEBVTT

1
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:35,911
Babe, what are you doing?

2
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:37,663
I'm looking for
the aloe iodine.

3
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:39,414
It's not here.

4
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:41,583
Yeah, because that's
not where it is.

5
00:00:43,836 --> 00:00:45,546
Babe, c-can you give me
12 seconds,

6
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:46,880
and I will come
and get it for you?

7
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:48,799
Twelve seconds is specific.

8
00:00:49,508 --> 00:00:51,176
Wow, these are very expired.

9
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,610
Hmm.

10
00:01:08,652 --> 00:01:11,613
Okay. Betadine.
Chlorhexidine.

11
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:13,282
No iodine.

12
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:16,910
Oh. Right. Thanks.

13
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:30,257
But...

14
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:32,050
Well, that's not...

15
00:01:33,594 --> 00:01:34,636
We tried for two years.

16
00:01:34,678 --> 00:01:37,472
I know. I know, babe.

17
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,474
I mean, we don't wanna even
talk about it anymore.

18
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:41,768
Talking was not
the important part.

19
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:46,648
It wasn't gonna be for us, and
we were okay with that.

20
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,109
- We were okay, but...
- Mm-hmm.

21
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,321
Well...

22
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:56,366
This is better.

23
00:01:57,326 --> 00:01:59,328
Yes. It's...

24
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:02,039
- It's a lot better, isn't it?
- This is great.

25
00:02:13,926 --> 00:02:15,469
Obviously,
we're gonna need protocols

26
00:02:15,511 --> 00:02:16,637
to account for
our cell mutations...

27
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:18,096
No, Reed.

28
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,389
...monitoring for
further cosmic effects.

29
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:20,474
Reed.

30
00:02:20,516 --> 00:02:22,059
We can do this.

31
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,478
Okay?

32
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,731
I really want to do this.

33
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,067
Then what?

34
00:02:34,947 --> 00:02:37,032
Nothing is going to change.

35
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:39,660
Of course not.

36
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:43,956
Ladies and gentlemen,

37
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,834
we welcome you
to a very special event

38
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:50,462
celebrating four years of
the Fantastic Four.

39
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:54,216
And now your host
for the evening, Ted Gilbert.

40
00:02:54,258 --> 00:02:56,635
Well, now, folks.

41
00:02:56,677 --> 00:02:59,221
Folks, we all know the story.

42
00:02:59,263 --> 00:03:02,224
Four brave astronauts
head up into space,

43
00:03:02,266 --> 00:03:04,268
encounter a bit of
cosmic turbulence,

44
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:05,853
and come back forever changed.

45
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:08,146
Not just the molecules
of their bodies

46
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:10,566
but also their place
in our hearts.

47
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:12,276
And, now, a look back.

48
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:14,069
This is
Excelsior Launch Control.

49
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:16,572
T-minus 3 hours, 42 minutes,
19 seconds.

50
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,574
Four years ago,

51
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:22,119
man and woman conquered the
last frontier as we know it,

52
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,496
the exploration of space.

53
00:03:25,998 --> 00:03:27,457
The best pilot in the world
right here.

54
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:29,793
Yeah. The best-looking
he means.

55
00:03:32,838 --> 00:03:36,425
It was my mission:
Space exploration.

56
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:38,010
I assembled the best
scientific minds

57
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:39,511
to come along,

58
00:03:39,553 --> 00:03:41,513
who also happened to be
my best friend,

59
00:03:42,181 --> 00:03:43,473
my wife

60
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:45,559
and my brother-in-law.

61
00:03:45,601 --> 00:03:47,644
Comms check.
Everybody, sound off.

62
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:49,396
- Check.
- Check, check.

63
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:51,607
- Check.
- Comms are live.

64
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:53,025
That last voice you just heard

65
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,568
was my baby brother,
Jonathan Storm,

66
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:57,863
and, ladies,
he is very single.

67
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,782
- Kiss for luck.
- Kiss?

68
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:05,537
However,
Dr. Richards's expedition

69
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:08,123
encountered
an unforeseen event

70
00:04:08,165 --> 00:04:10,042
that changed
not only the lives

71
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,627
of these
courageous individuals...

72
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,128
Verify go for launch.

73
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,963
Go for launch.

74
00:04:15,005 --> 00:04:17,090
...but also
the course of our history.

75
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:18,550
- Come in, Excelsior.
- What is that?

76
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:19,676
I don't know. I don't know.

77
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:22,638
It must be the cosmic rays.

78
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:24,556
- Ben! Ben!
- Ben!

79
00:04:25,641 --> 00:04:27,476
Obviously,
while we were in space

80
00:04:27,518 --> 00:04:28,769
due to errors on my part...

81
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,187
- Stop.
- ...we encountered

82
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:32,356
a cosmic storm
that altered our DNA.

83
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:34,233
Rescue in progress
of the Excelsior launch.

84
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,984
We came back with anomalies.

85
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:40,948
And they
returned with superpowers.

86
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:54,253
They became our protectors.

87
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:03,595
Cannonball!

88
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:19,903
It's clobberin' time!

89
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:33,876
Hmm.

90
00:05:45,012 --> 00:05:47,306
I was at the opening
of the Pan Am Tower

91
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:49,016
when Mole Man attacked.

92
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:52,394
The Fantastic Four
saved my life.

93
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:07,284
Mole Man's attempt
to steal the Pan Am building

94
00:06:07,326 --> 00:06:09,620
was thwarted
by the Fantastic Four.

95
00:06:09,661 --> 00:06:11,747
This is all
Reed Richards's fault.

96
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,208
Him and his endless pursuit
of progress.

97
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:16,668
Power to the underground!

98
00:06:20,923 --> 00:06:22,382
And when the Mad Thinker

99
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:24,968
tried to sabotage
New York City

100
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:28,347
the Fantastic Four
came to our rescue.

101
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,225
Gotcha!

102
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:35,854
Have a great day!

103
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,067
They defeated Red Ghost

104
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,860
and his Super-Apes.

105
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:54,957
They became our inspiration.

106
00:06:54,998 --> 00:06:58,961
This equation not only
confirms alternate dimensions,

107
00:06:59,002 --> 00:07:01,088
but it suggests
parallel Earths

108
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:03,590
exist on different
dimensional planes.

109
00:07:06,218 --> 00:07:07,845
Who wants to see
a big explosion?

110
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,179
Me!

111
00:07:11,265 --> 00:07:13,058
And they became our leaders.

112
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,185
Sue Storm brokers
peace deal

113
00:07:15,227 --> 00:07:17,271
with Harvey "Mole Man" Elder,

114
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:20,399
leader of the underground
nation, Subterranea.

115
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,025
I don't trust
surface dwellers.

116
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,151
I never have.

117
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:25,654
But I do trust Sue.

118
00:07:25,696 --> 00:07:29,867
We have come together today
to form a new charter,

119
00:07:29,908 --> 00:07:31,410
the Future Foundation.

120
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:33,620
All participating
countries agree

121
00:07:33,662 --> 00:07:36,623
to dismantle
their armed forces.

122
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:38,625
And on
this fourth anniversary,

123
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:39,835
we celebrate them.

124
00:07:39,877 --> 00:07:41,962
They are the very best of us.

125
00:07:42,004 --> 00:07:44,506
They are the Fantastic Four.

126
00:07:44,548 --> 00:07:49,928
Thank you, Fantastic Four!

127
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:51,471
- Thank you, Fantastic Four!
- We love you, Fantastic Four.

128
00:07:51,513 --> 00:07:53,390
- I love you, Johnny!
- We love you!

129
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:56,977
- Thank you, Fantastic Four.
- Thank you, Fantastic Four.

130
00:07:58,437 --> 00:08:00,814
We are proud to
call them our guides,

131
00:08:01,014 --> 00:08:03,108
our protectors
and our friends.

132
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:06,653
Let's hear it for Reed, Sue,
Johnny and Ben.

133
00:08:14,453 --> 00:08:16,496
I must say, that
was all a bit aggrandizing.

134
00:08:16,538 --> 00:08:18,207
- Yeah.
- H.E.R.B.I.E.

135
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:19,875
H.E.R.B.I.E. with the herbs.

136
00:08:19,917 --> 00:08:21,460
How's that sauce looking?

137
00:08:21,502 --> 00:08:23,754
Don't do that.
Wash your hands first, please.

138
00:08:23,795 --> 00:08:25,130
I was wearing my gloves
the whole time.

139
00:08:25,172 --> 00:08:26,590
Just wash your hands.
Let me try that.

140
00:08:29,218 --> 00:08:30,511
Okay.

141
00:08:31,345 --> 00:08:34,598
Okay. Is this guy good?

142
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,975
That is fantastic.

143
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:39,186
- Oh, let me try.
- It's incredible stuff.

144
00:08:39,228 --> 00:08:40,854
Stop. Don't do that.

145
00:08:40,896 --> 00:08:42,940
Don't do that.
It's not quite done.

146
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:44,149
No, it's not quite done.

147
00:08:44,191 --> 00:08:45,651
No, it could be done,

148
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:47,110
but I'm gonna add
a little more garlic.

149
00:08:47,152 --> 00:08:48,695
Not because
it's not delicious.

150
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:51,532
I just want to add
a little bit of zip, okay?

151
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:57,204
What are you doing?

152
00:08:57,246 --> 00:08:59,206
What do you mean,
what am I doing?

153
00:08:59,248 --> 00:09:00,874
I mean, you're gonna
ruin your appetite.

154
00:09:00,916 --> 00:09:03,335
I'm hungry.

155
00:09:05,546 --> 00:09:07,381
They're never late
for Sunday dinner.

156
00:09:07,422 --> 00:09:08,966
Should we wait?

157
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,968
I guess.

158
00:09:11,009 --> 00:09:12,261
You're late.

159
00:09:14,471 --> 00:09:15,931
What, uh- What do you mean?

160
00:09:15,973 --> 00:09:17,099
What do you mean,
what do I mean?

161
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,475
You're late for dinner.

162
00:09:18,517 --> 00:09:20,060
Oh. Yes, we are.
We're late for dinner.

163
00:09:20,102 --> 00:09:21,812
- By a single minute.
- Yes, we were just...

164
00:09:21,854 --> 00:09:24,523
I had to put some aloe iodine
on my shoulder and...

165
00:09:24,565 --> 00:09:26,233
...just had to do
his shoulder and...

166
00:09:26,275 --> 00:09:27,860
Why is there breakfast cereal
on the dinner table?

167
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:29,444
Why are you being weird?

168
00:09:29,486 --> 00:09:32,281
- We're not being weird.
- We're not acting weird.

169
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:34,324
You're doing that
weird thing with your face.

170
00:09:34,366 --> 00:09:36,285
Well, we don't know
what you're talking about.

171
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:40,205
Are you pregnant?

172
00:09:45,878 --> 00:09:47,838
- Yeah, we're pregnant.
- Yes, yes.

173
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,298
How did you know that?

174
00:09:49,339 --> 00:09:50,883
Have you looked at
your husband's face?

175
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,217
I know.
He just cannot keep a secret.

176
00:09:52,259 --> 00:09:54,303
- Wait, what? Really?
- Yeah.

177
00:09:55,804 --> 00:09:58,599
What?

178
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:02,686
You are gonna be the best mom.
Oh, my God.

179
00:10:02,728 --> 00:10:04,605
And you are gonna be
the best dad.

180
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:06,899
Just kidding.
You are out of your depth.

181
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:09,610
But we... we're gonna be
the best uncles ever.

182
00:10:11,028 --> 00:10:12,446
Okay, we should eat.

183
00:10:14,281 --> 00:10:16,033
You're handling this well,
you know.

184
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:17,659
I figured you'd be
locked in your lab

185
00:10:17,701 --> 00:10:19,745
drenched in a panic sweat.

186
00:10:19,786 --> 00:10:21,413
I have that
scheduled for later.

187
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,041
Countdown continues

188
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:25,751
as the Fantastic Four
prepare to welcome

189
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:27,836
a new member to the family.

190
00:10:27,878 --> 00:10:31,507
Needless to say, preparations
inside the Baxter Building

191
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:33,592
are well underway.

192
00:10:33,634 --> 00:10:36,720
All right, H.E.R.B.I.E.,
let's start the baby prep.

193
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:57,950
H.E.R.B.I.E.!

194
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:05,040
Yancy Street bookies

195
00:11:05,082 --> 00:11:06,959
are putting the odds
of a girl at 4-to-5,

196
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,919
but chances of twins
are a long shot.

197
00:11:14,508 --> 00:11:16,218
Herbert!

198
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:28,146
H.E.R.B.I.E.!

199
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:29,273
The oil and gas cowboys

200
00:11:29,356 --> 00:11:30,774
want a minute to yell at you

201
00:11:30,816 --> 00:11:32,609
before you go
on maternity leave.

202
00:11:32,651 --> 00:11:35,654
Speaking of, coal lobby.

203
00:11:35,696 --> 00:11:37,114
Lynne, when you see Sue, can-

204
00:11:37,155 --> 00:11:39,241
Larry, I will tell her
when I see her.

205
00:11:39,283 --> 00:11:40,659
Thank you, Lynne.

206
00:11:40,701 --> 00:11:42,536
The question
on everybody's mind is,

207
00:11:42,578 --> 00:11:45,539
"Will the baby be born
with superpowers?"

208
00:11:46,707 --> 00:11:48,125
H.E.R.B.I.E.,
we need to scan the baby.

209
00:11:48,167 --> 00:11:50,085
The Interna-Scan
hasn't achieved

210
00:11:50,127 --> 00:11:52,629
the right level of precession
for clear imaging.

211
00:11:55,007 --> 00:11:57,926
New deep space transmission?

212
00:11:57,968 --> 00:11:59,636
Let's identify its origin.

213
00:11:59,678 --> 00:12:01,638
Shall we record and file it?

214
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:03,056
Mm-hmm.

215
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:10,272
2:15? What 2:15? I don't have
any meetings today.

216
00:12:11,398 --> 00:12:12,900
Ah, Reed.

217
00:12:12,941 --> 00:12:14,860
Oh, that 2:15.

218
00:12:14,902 --> 00:12:16,153
Thank you for making the time.

219
00:12:16,195 --> 00:12:17,738
Johnny, do we have to today?

220
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:19,740
I had some thoughts
on the new suit design.

221
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:21,617
There are no new suit designs.

222
00:12:21,658 --> 00:12:25,120
You finished them years ago.
They have dust on them.

223
00:12:27,456 --> 00:12:29,416
I get it. You're going
to be a father soon.

224
00:12:29,458 --> 00:12:30,792
New responsibilities.

225
00:12:30,834 --> 00:12:31,793
- You're a bit scared.
- I'm not scared.

226
00:12:31,835 --> 00:12:33,337
I'm busy, Johnny.

227
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:35,380
I'm busy. I'm busy.

228
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:37,216
There's a difference.

229
00:12:40,761 --> 00:12:43,138
New transmission today.

230
00:12:44,139 --> 00:12:45,516
Have you listened to it yet?

231
00:12:45,557 --> 00:12:47,559
More of the same.
It's a complex signal.

232
00:12:50,187 --> 00:12:52,231
Knock yourself out.

233
00:12:53,732 --> 00:12:56,360
Johnny, I'm running a test.

234
00:12:57,069 --> 00:12:58,403
Cool.

235
00:13:00,656 --> 00:13:01,949
I got time.

236
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,077
Bridge teleportation test.

237
00:13:07,246 --> 00:13:10,374
Movement of organic matter,
six meters.

238
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,545
Thank you, Herbert.

239
00:13:16,505 --> 00:13:17,756
Let's run it.

240
00:13:26,056 --> 00:13:27,558
It worked.

241
00:13:30,853 --> 00:13:32,855
- Johnny.
- Yep.

242
00:13:34,106 --> 00:13:35,315
Could you reset the breaker?

243
00:13:40,946 --> 00:13:41,989
Other way.

244
00:14:16,523 --> 00:14:17,649
Babe?

245
00:14:19,109 --> 00:14:20,944
Babe, when you're done,
can you...

246
00:14:23,989 --> 00:14:25,949
Hello, H.E.R.B.I.E.

247
00:14:28,327 --> 00:14:31,330
I, um...
I just went by the nursery.

248
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:34,124
How's it looking?

249
00:14:34,166 --> 00:14:36,418
Um, it's looking like

250
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,128
H.E.R.B.I.E.'s
building the crib.

251
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:40,672
Which I kinda thought
was a you deal.

252
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:42,216
I built this instead.

253
00:14:42,257 --> 00:14:45,177
Anyone can build a crib.
Only I can build this.

254
00:14:45,219 --> 00:14:48,555
Anyone can build a crib
but not-not ours. Not for him.

255
00:14:48,597 --> 00:14:50,015
This is for him.

256
00:14:52,226 --> 00:14:53,685
Because unlike anyone else,

257
00:14:53,727 --> 00:14:55,395
his parents have
cosmically compromised DNA.

258
00:14:55,437 --> 00:14:59,399
Reed.
Reed, we have done every test.

259
00:15:00,317 --> 00:15:01,944
Well, not this one.

260
00:15:04,279 --> 00:15:05,531
You wanna see?

261
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:09,993
Fine. Let's see.

262
00:15:35,018 --> 00:15:37,938
See? There's
nothing wrong with him.

