Go for launch.

524
00:30:11,019 --> 00:30:13,480
...two, one.

525
00:30:29,913 --> 00:30:31,915
The Excelsior has liftoff.

526
00:30:47,556 --> 00:30:49,725
Whoo-hoo!

527
00:30:55,063 --> 00:30:57,149
Ladies and gentlemen,

528
00:30:57,191 --> 00:30:59,234
we have a successful launch.

529
00:31:03,697 --> 00:31:05,449
And from all of us on Earth,

530
00:31:06,158 --> 00:31:07,701
we wish you good luck.

531
00:31:08,327 --> 00:31:09,536
And Godspeed.

532
00:31:11,205 --> 00:31:12,915
Thank you, Earth.

533
00:31:18,504 --> 00:31:19,755
You seeing that?

534
00:31:23,425 --> 00:31:25,302
Approaching the FTL engine.

535
00:31:40,192 --> 00:31:41,485
Wait for my signal, Sue.

536
00:31:41,527 --> 00:31:42,861
Yeah.

537
00:31:42,903 --> 00:31:46,573
And three, two, one. Mark.

538
00:31:54,957 --> 00:31:58,877
And we are locked.

539
00:32:00,212 --> 00:32:02,548
And clear for FTL navigation.

540
00:32:02,589 --> 00:32:06,844
Faster-than-light
in three, two, one.

541
00:32:18,689 --> 00:32:21,108
So the herald's
energy signature tracks

542
00:32:21,149 --> 00:32:23,360
to this binary system here.

543
00:32:23,402 --> 00:32:26,488
LHS-275, yes.

544
00:32:26,530 --> 00:32:29,074
Where we find her,
we find Galactus.

545
00:32:29,116 --> 00:32:30,993
Reed, what are
we up against here?

546
00:32:31,034 --> 00:32:33,579
Some sort of a space dragon
or something?

547
00:32:33,620 --> 00:32:35,247
- Cool.
- We don't know.

548
00:32:35,289 --> 00:32:36,999
But it's
basic tactical science.

549
00:32:37,040 --> 00:32:39,418
Observe, assess capabilities,
have H.E.R.B.I.E. collect

550
00:32:39,459 --> 00:32:40,752
any liquid, gas...

551
00:32:40,794 --> 00:32:42,129
...solid materials,

552
00:32:42,171 --> 00:32:43,547
analyze his physiology.

553
00:32:45,841 --> 00:32:47,885
Look, if he's just
some big guy in a ship,

554
00:32:47,926 --> 00:32:49,428
then yes,
you can punch him out.

555
00:33:00,606 --> 00:33:02,900
Coming in on the dark side
of the system's larger planet.

556
00:33:02,941 --> 00:33:05,235
Copy that.
I'm gonna take us out of FTL.

557
00:33:05,277 --> 00:33:07,237
Okay, everyone. Be prepared.

558
00:33:13,994 --> 00:33:15,454
So, where's this Galactus?

559
00:33:20,250 --> 00:33:22,211
That's strange.

560
00:33:22,252 --> 00:33:25,422
The herald's heat signature is
coming from inside the planet.

561
00:33:30,135 --> 00:33:32,095
What the hell is happening
to that planet?

562
00:33:32,137 --> 00:33:33,639
Is there something alive
down there?

563
00:33:44,983 --> 00:33:46,360
What is that?

564
00:33:48,570 --> 00:33:50,155
- Ben!
- I'm on it!

565
00:33:50,197 --> 00:33:52,157
Dropping us out of FTL.

566
00:33:56,620 --> 00:33:57,788
Watch out!

567
00:34:03,043 --> 00:34:04,169
Sue, hide us!

568
00:34:22,479 --> 00:34:25,315
It's all gone.
The whole planet.

569
00:34:25,357 --> 00:34:27,651
And it was 13%
larger than Earth.

570
00:34:33,115 --> 00:34:34,741
- Ben!
- It's not responding.

571
00:34:34,783 --> 00:34:35,659
I'm locked out.

572
00:34:37,911 --> 00:34:40,622
H.E.R.B.I.E., try to stabilize
the engines.

573
00:34:42,374 --> 00:34:43,667
What's going on?

574
00:34:43,709 --> 00:34:45,252
It's got us.
It's pulling us in.

575
00:34:45,294 --> 00:34:46,962
Ben, save the engines.

576
00:34:48,088 --> 00:34:49,381
Save the engine!

577
00:35:23,540 --> 00:35:24,583
Johnny...

578
00:35:26,710 --> 00:35:28,086
your girlfriend's back.

579
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:40,807
Hi.

580
00:35:40,849 --> 00:35:43,101
Galactus will see you.

581
00:35:43,143 --> 00:35:45,687
- I'll go.
- All of you.

582
00:35:47,773 --> 00:35:49,191
You should not have come.

583
00:36:29,147 --> 00:36:30,482
Follow.

584
00:36:31,567 --> 00:36:33,193
Scan everything
and collect samples.

585
00:36:46,039 --> 00:36:47,541
What does Galactus want?

586
00:36:48,876 --> 00:36:51,628
He doesn't want. He feeds.

587
00:36:53,755 --> 00:36:56,175
How does he choose
which planets to consume?

588
00:36:56,675 --> 00:36:58,218
He does not.

589
00:37:00,012 --> 00:37:01,346
You choose.

590
00:37:02,723 --> 00:37:03,765
Yes.

591
00:37:06,852 --> 00:37:09,396
Uh, Johnny.
What are you doing?

592
00:37:09,438 --> 00:37:10,856
I'm gonna charm her.

593
00:37:14,902 --> 00:37:16,820
So what did you say to me?

594
00:37:16,862 --> 00:37:18,572
When you threw me
off your board?

595
00:37:19,781 --> 00:37:20,991
What did you say?

596
00:37:24,912 --> 00:37:26,705
It's a blessing.

597
00:37:26,747 --> 00:37:29,958
It means, "Die with yours."

598
00:37:31,418 --> 00:37:33,504
"Die with yours."

599
00:37:35,631 --> 00:37:36,840
Last question.

600
00:37:36,882 --> 00:37:38,759
So the surfboard, right?

601
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:40,469
Is that part of your body?
Or is that...

602
00:37:49,144 --> 00:37:50,521
So she dumped you already?

603
00:37:50,562 --> 00:37:51,730
No. It went well.

604
00:38:07,454 --> 00:38:09,957
You stand before Galactus.

605
00:38:18,590 --> 00:38:21,468
The Devourer of Worlds
honors you.

606
00:38:31,979 --> 00:38:33,230
We are honored.

607
00:38:34,898 --> 00:38:38,152
I was once little like you.

608
00:38:38,861 --> 00:38:41,405
Billions of years ago.

609
00:38:42,156 --> 00:38:44,741
A man from another world

610
00:38:45,742 --> 00:38:50,664
before this relentless,
eternal hunger.

611
00:38:54,626 --> 00:38:56,670
You have traveled far.

612
00:38:59,298 --> 00:39:00,674
Yes.

613
00:39:03,343 --> 00:39:06,013
To beg for mercy.

614
00:39:07,931 --> 00:39:09,391
To talk.

615
00:39:10,392 --> 00:39:13,979
You carry the power
to save your world.

616
00:39:14,021 --> 00:39:15,522
Yes. I believe we do.

617
00:39:16,273 --> 00:39:17,816
Inside her.

618
00:39:18,984 --> 00:39:20,402
The child.

619
00:39:22,571 --> 00:39:24,239
- What the hell?
- What...

620
00:39:24,740 --> 00:39:26,617
He hungers.

621
00:39:26,658 --> 00:39:28,118
What does that mean?

622
00:39:28,160 --> 00:39:30,787
I will spare your world.

623
00:39:31,622 --> 00:39:33,457
In exchange for the boy.

624
00:39:33,499 --> 00:39:35,834
What? No.

625
00:39:35,876 --> 00:39:39,296
He possesses the Power Cosmic,

626
00:39:39,338 --> 00:39:42,674
and he will inherit
this cursed throne.

627
00:39:43,592 --> 00:39:46,303
It's not true.
He's- He's normal.

628
00:39:46,345 --> 00:39:49,556
We would know. I would know.
I tested the child.

629
00:39:49,598 --> 00:39:52,684
- He hides his nature from you.
- No.

630
00:40:03,654 --> 00:40:05,113
What are you doing to her?

631
00:40:05,155 --> 00:40:07,074
Baby's coming.
The baby's coming.

632
00:40:07,115 --> 00:40:08,367
- Now?
- Yeah.

633
00:40:08,408 --> 00:40:11,036
You will not have our planet.

634
00:40:11,078 --> 00:40:12,996
And you will never have
our son!

635
00:40:22,047 --> 00:40:24,758
I will eat your planet slowly

636
00:40:25,843 --> 00:40:28,554
while your child watches.

637
00:40:54,997 --> 00:40:56,165
No you don't!

638
00:41:06,758 --> 00:41:08,010
I'm coming, buddy!

639
00:41:10,179 --> 00:41:11,221
Go, go, go, go!

640
00:41:12,389 --> 00:41:14,892
H.E.R.B.I.E., prep all systems
for immediate launch.

641
00:41:20,981 --> 00:41:23,484
No!

642
00:41:30,073 --> 00:41:31,575
No!

643
00:41:36,580 --> 00:41:39,291
Surfboard,
not part of the body.

644
00:41:48,884 --> 00:41:50,385
Come on.

645
00:42:03,857 --> 00:42:04,900
H.E.R.B.I.E.!

646
00:42:04,942 --> 00:42:06,193
Come on.

647
00:42:09,071 --> 00:42:10,489
Get us out of here, Ben!

648
00:42:10,531 --> 00:42:12,407
Hang in there, Suze,
I'll get you home.

649
00:42:27,714 --> 00:42:29,424
Get us to the FTL!

650
00:42:30,926 --> 00:42:32,261
FTL in visual range.

651
00:42:32,302 --> 00:42:34,847
- Babe.
- I'm here, Sue. I'm here.

652
00:42:37,516 --> 00:42:38,517
Surfer on our six.

653
00:42:39,393 --> 00:42:40,894
Attach then jump.

654
00:42:40,936 --> 00:42:43,480
- And go where?
- Anywhere! Just jump!

655
00:42:46,567 --> 00:42:48,652
H.E.R.B.I.E.,
I'm gonna need your help

656
00:42:48,694 --> 00:42:49,653
stabilizing this thing.

657
00:43:00,330 --> 00:43:02,082
Hold on!

658
00:43:12,301 --> 00:43:14,595
Ben!

659
00:43:22,436 --> 00:43:24,354
We lost her. All clear.

660
00:43:31,445 --> 00:43:32,654
She's still on us.

661
00:43:32,696 --> 00:43:33,697
Johnny, kill her.

662
00:43:33,739 --> 00:43:35,115
- Really?
- Yeah.

663
00:43:35,157 --> 00:43:36,575
She wants to take your nephew.

664
00:43:36,617 --> 00:43:38,619
- Kill her!
- All right. All right.

665
00:43:40,746 --> 00:43:44,374
Just when I finally met
someone interesting.

666
00:43:53,800 --> 00:43:55,469
It's bending the beam!

667
00:43:55,511 --> 00:43:57,888
The wormhole
is bending the beam!

668
00:44:03,310 --> 00:44:05,646
Reed,
I can't get a lock on her!

669
00:44:05,687 --> 00:44:07,314
All right. Figure it out.
Come on.

670
00:44:07,356 --> 00:44:08,607
Reed, what's the plan?

671
00:44:17,407 --> 00:44:18,784
Johnny, quit screwing around.

672
00:44:18,826 --> 00:44:20,160
Do I tell you
how to drive the ship?

673
00:44:20,202 --> 00:44:22,204
Don't tell me
how to kill sexy aliens!

674
00:44:22,246 --> 00:44:23,705
Stop calling her sexy.

675
00:44:28,210 --> 00:44:30,295
- Oh!
- Yes! Yes!

676
00:44:30,337 --> 00:44:31,380
- Yes!
- Yes!

677
00:44:37,511 --> 00:44:38,929
She's back!

678
00:44:38,971 --> 00:44:40,556
- Reed, I can't shake her.
- Working on it!

679
00:44:42,182 --> 00:44:44,142
- She's slippery!
- Reed!

680
00:44:48,605 --> 00:44:50,399
Drop us out of FTL here.

681
00:44:50,440 --> 00:44:52,192
That's a pretty big
neutron star.

682
00:44:52,234 --> 00:44:53,944
I know. We're gonna use it.

683
00:44:53,986 --> 00:44:55,863
Isn't that basically
a black hole?

684
00:44:56,446 --> 00:44:57,489
Won't that kill us?

685
00:44:57,531 --> 00:44:58,740
Taking us out.

686
00:45:18,302 --> 00:45:19,636
What's the plan?

687
00:45:19,678 --> 00:45:20,971
Draw her close enough
to the star,

688
00:45:21,013 --> 00:45:22,598
she'll get stuck
in the gravity well.

689
00:45:22,639 --> 00:45:24,141
There'll be a time dilation.

690
00:45:24,183 --> 00:45:26,310
- How much of a dilation?
- Is it more than mine?

691
00:45:26,351 --> 00:45:28,020
It'll take her a month
to break free.

692
00:45:29,855 --> 00:45:31,064
Take us in, Ben.

693
00:45:31,106 --> 00:45:32,774
Reed, we could get sucked in.

694
00:45:33,400 --> 00:45:34,568
Ben, trust me.

695
00:45:35,194 --> 00:45:36,278
Hang on.

696
00:45:50,667 --> 00:45:51,793
Come on.

697
00:45:51,835 --> 00:45:52,794
It's chewing us up!

698
00:45:54,004 --> 00:45:55,130
Get closer.

699
00:45:55,172 --> 00:45:56,465
It's chewing us up!

700
00:45:56,507 --> 00:45:58,175
A little closer!

701
00:45:59,176 --> 00:46:00,928
Come on, Reed.
What are we doing?

702
00:46:00,969 --> 00:46:04,056
Sue, we need 30 seconds of
invisibility. Can you do it?

703
00:46:04,097 --> 00:46:05,933
After your next contraction.

704
00:46:54,314 --> 00:46:55,941
- Yes!
- Hell, yeah!

705
00:46:55,983 --> 00:46:59,570
You all right, Sue?

706
00:47:00,445 --> 00:47:01,947
We need to strap you down.

707
00:47:01,989 --> 00:47:04,449
- Strapping her down.
- Do not strap me down!

708
00:47:05,450 --> 00:47:06,952
Not strapping her down.

709
00:47:06,994 --> 00:47:08,662
Baby...

710
00:47:08,704 --> 00:47:10,414
- What?
- ...you need gravity to push.

711
00:47:10,455 --> 00:47:11,790
This is not right.

712
00:47:11,832 --> 00:47:13,041
It's not how
it's supposed to be.

713
00:47:13,083 --> 00:47:14,418
I know, I know.

714
00:47:14,459 --> 00:47:15,794
But we're gonna make it work.

715
00:47:17,379 --> 00:47:18,922
You're doing wonderful,
my love.

716
00:47:22,301 --> 00:47:24,344
We don't have enough juice
to get home.

717
00:47:24,386 --> 00:47:25,762
Oh, no.

718
00:47:29,474 --> 00:47:30,642
No, we do not.

719
00:47:30,684 --> 00:47:32,477
I could slingshot
around the star,

720
00:47:32,519 --> 00:47:34,062
draft off
its orbital momentum.

721
00:47:34,104 --> 00:47:36,565
We need to get to
.88 speed of light.

722
00:47:36,607 --> 00:47:38,275
Reed!

723
00:47:38,317 --> 00:47:39,943
- Johnny, the velocity gauge.
- Reed!

724
00:47:39,985 --> 00:47:41,069
On it.

725
00:47:42,029 --> 00:47:43,780
- Oh, don't... don't go.
- I'm here.

726
00:47:43,822 --> 00:47:45,407
- I'm not going anywhere.
- Don't go.

727
00:47:45,449 --> 00:47:47,117
I'm right here.

728
00:47:47,159 --> 00:47:49,203
Beginning slingshot.
Here we go.

729
00:47:52,039 --> 00:47:53,457
Coming up on .82.

730
00:47:53,499 --> 00:47:54,666
On your mark, Johnny.

731
00:47:56,418 --> 00:47:57,961
Why...
Why do they wanna take him?

732
00:47:58,003 --> 00:47:59,213
Something is wrong with him.

733
00:47:59,254 --> 00:48:00,797
There's nothing wrong
with him.

734
00:48:00,839 --> 00:48:02,174
- You don't know that.
- Yes, I do. I do know.

735
00:48:02,216 --> 00:48:03,091
No, you don't.
You know everything,

736
00:48:03,133 --> 00:48:04,593
but you don't know that.

737
00:48:04,635 --> 00:48:06,303
- What if he's a monster?
- He's not a monster.

738
00:48:06,345 --> 00:48:08,305
- Everything's gonna change.
- Nothing is gonna change.

739
00:48:08,347 --> 00:48:10,015
- Everything's gonna change.
- I promise you.

740
00:48:10,057 --> 00:48:11,808
- I promise.
- You can't promise that.

741
00:48:11,850 --> 00:48:13,352
- I promise.
- You can't promise that.

742
00:48:13,393 --> 00:48:14,978
- Reed...
- Okay.

743
00:48:19,149 --> 00:48:20,984
He's coming. He's coming.

744
00:48:21,026 --> 00:48:22,069
Give me your hand.

745
00:48:22,110 --> 00:48:23,320
.84. Ben!

746
00:48:23,362 --> 00:48:24,738
Come on!

747
00:48:27,366 --> 00:48:28,992
- Sue? Push.
- No.

748
00:48:29,034 --> 00:48:30,661
- Yes, you can.
- .85.

749
00:48:30,702 --> 00:48:31,829
- Ready?
- Okay.

750
00:48:31,870 --> 00:48:34,414
One, two, three, push!

751
00:48:37,876 --> 00:48:40,420
- Come on!
- .86!

752
00:48:40,462 --> 00:48:42,756
Push. Push. That's good.

753
00:48:44,216 --> 00:48:45,300
.87.

754
00:48:48,846 --> 00:48:50,389
- Mark!
- Ben!

755
00:48:50,430 --> 00:48:52,224
H.E.R.B.I.E.

756
00:48:53,642 --> 00:48:55,686
Ben, help!

757
00:48:55,727 --> 00:48:57,187
Thrusters engaged.

758
00:48:58,689 --> 00:49:00,107
H.E.R.B.I.E., get ready!

759
00:49:05,904 --> 00:49:07,322
Hold on, everyone.

760
00:49:32,222 --> 00:49:35,017
I got you, little guy.

761
00:50:05,923 --> 00:50:06,965
Franklin.

762
00:50:37,079 --> 00:50:39,373
There! There! Come on.
I see it!

763
00:50:48,507 --> 00:50:49,842
Wow!

764
00:51:08,402 --> 00:51:10,571
After a monthlong return trip,

765
00:51:10,612 --> 00:51:12,906
the Fantastic Four
are finally home

766
00:51:12,948 --> 00:51:14,533
and receiving a warm welcome.

767
00:51:27,462 --> 00:51:29,798
Oh, my God. Unbelievable.

768
00:51:29,840 --> 00:51:31,884
- Lynne, we're going to need-
- Come this way.

769
00:51:35,679 --> 00:51:37,472
- Reed! Reed!
- Move back!

770
00:51:37,514 --> 00:51:39,850
Dr. Richards,
over here! Can we get a word?

771
00:51:39,892 --> 00:51:42,019
Stand back.
Make a path.

772
00:51:42,060 --> 00:51:44,563
Sue! Sue!

773
00:51:48,984 --> 00:51:50,944
They're ready
for you. Step up.

774
00:51:51,144 --> 00:51:52,029
Just keep it brief.

775
00:51:56,783 --> 00:51:58,911
I'm sorry. We don't have
a prepared statement.

776
00:52:01,997 --> 00:52:04,208
One at a time, please.
One at a time.

777
00:52:04,249 --> 00:52:05,584
Connor.

778
00:52:05,626 --> 00:52:07,252
Welcome back.

779
00:52:07,294 --> 00:52:09,087
Could you take us through
how you defeated Galactus?

780
00:52:10,756 --> 00:52:11,798
How we de...

781
00:52:15,177 --> 00:52:16,887
We didn't.

782
00:52:16,929 --> 00:52:19,056
Not yet. Not yet, we didn't.

783
00:52:19,097 --> 00:52:20,140
What does that mean?

784
00:52:20,182 --> 00:52:21,683
Uh, follow up!

785
00:52:23,727 --> 00:52:25,145
What do you mean, you didn't?

786
00:52:26,688 --> 00:52:29,858
We attempted to negotiate,
but Galactus...

787
00:52:33,362 --> 00:52:35,823
He asked too high a price.

788
00:52:35,864 --> 00:52:38,158
- Well, what does he want?
- What did he ask?

789
00:52:42,162 --> 00:52:43,747
