01:06:49,676 --> 01:06:50,719
For how long?

1046
01:06:51,887 --> 01:06:54,181
Factoring in we gotta
keep building bridges,

1047
01:06:54,223 --> 01:06:57,184
how long would we need
to conserve power?

1048
01:06:58,685 --> 01:07:01,063
Sacrifices
will be made.

1049
01:07:01,104 --> 01:07:04,024
We all need to conserve power at
a scale never attempted before.

1050
01:07:04,066 --> 01:07:06,485
Quite right, H.E.R.B.I.E.

1051
01:07:06,527 --> 01:07:08,779
All the power.

1052
01:07:08,821 --> 01:07:11,824
The worldwide energy curfew
only works

1053
01:07:11,865 --> 01:07:14,284
if everybody does their part
to conserve electricity.

1054
01:07:19,456 --> 01:07:21,708
Ooh, missed a spot.

1055
01:07:21,750 --> 01:07:24,294
Yeah, curfew fried it.

1056
01:07:24,336 --> 01:07:25,879
Now I look like an idiot.

1057
01:07:28,257 --> 01:07:29,341
Beard could be cool.

1058
01:07:31,009 --> 01:07:32,052
Seriously?

1059
01:07:33,595 --> 01:07:35,472
I built this to see
what you looked like.

1060
01:07:36,682 --> 01:07:38,433
You see,

1061
01:07:38,475 --> 01:07:41,770
most fathers want their sons
to look exactly like them,

1062
01:07:42,604 --> 01:07:43,939
inside and out.

1063
01:07:44,940 --> 01:07:45,983
But...

1064
01:07:47,401 --> 01:07:48,944
I don't want you
to be like me.

1065
01:07:52,364 --> 01:07:54,783
There's something wrong
with me, always has been.

1066
01:07:59,413 --> 01:08:00,914
The more I look at you,

1067
01:08:02,749 --> 01:08:04,042
the less I know.

1068
01:08:05,335 --> 01:08:07,546
And the less I know,
the more scared I am.

1069
01:08:09,840 --> 01:08:13,135
So you know what?
I'm not gonna look anymore.

1070
01:08:15,387 --> 01:08:18,474
I'm gonna let you tell me
who you are.

1071
01:08:18,515 --> 01:08:21,351
And if you'd like to tell me
now, that would be helpful,

1072
01:08:21,393 --> 01:08:24,396
especially if you're
an all-powerful space god.

1073
01:08:24,438 --> 01:08:27,774
I'd like to know that sooner rather
than later, if you don't mind.

1074
01:08:30,652 --> 01:08:31,987
Hmm.

1075
01:08:32,029 --> 01:08:33,739
Oh, no.

1076
01:08:33,780 --> 01:08:35,449
You're busy peeing.

1077
01:08:36,700 --> 01:08:38,035
You're a very good boy.

1078
01:08:47,711 --> 01:08:49,838
Thanks, buddy.

1079
01:08:55,344 --> 01:08:57,304
This is going to work.

1080
01:08:58,847 --> 01:08:59,890
It has to.

1081
01:09:32,798 --> 01:09:35,050
Yes! Yes!

1082
01:09:35,884 --> 01:09:37,886
Uh... Oh.

1083
01:09:37,928 --> 01:09:39,763
Yep, coming.
Coming, coming, coming.

1084
01:09:41,014 --> 01:09:44,351
Guys, I am onto something.

1085
01:09:44,393 --> 01:09:45,811
Moving a planet here, Johnny.

1086
01:09:45,853 --> 01:09:48,981
Yeah, Johnny. It's four.
Fantastic Four.

1087
01:09:49,022 --> 01:09:50,440
Let's move a planet.

1088
01:09:50,482 --> 01:09:52,609
- Cool beard.
- You mean that? Thank you.

1089
01:09:53,819 --> 01:09:55,404
Copy, Delhi.

1090
01:09:56,405 --> 01:09:57,447
Let's do this.

1091
01:09:57,489 --> 01:09:58,490
London, stand by.

1092
01:09:58,532 --> 01:09:59,908
Yes, copy, London.

1093
01:10:01,243 --> 01:10:02,536
Copy, Paris.

1094
01:10:02,578 --> 01:10:05,038
- Lima, do you copy?
- Copy, Rome.

1095
01:10:05,080 --> 01:10:07,374
- Copy, Delhi.
- Copy, Vienna.

1096
01:10:07,416 --> 01:10:08,917
Copy, Prague.

1097
01:10:08,959 --> 01:10:10,169
Chicago, stand by.

1098
01:10:10,210 --> 01:10:11,545
Copy, Chicago.

1099
01:10:12,796 --> 01:10:14,214
Earth go for countdown.

1100
01:10:15,048 --> 01:10:16,800
Here we go, folks.

1101
01:10:16,842 --> 01:10:18,552
Go.

1102
01:10:18,594 --> 01:10:21,555
20, 19...

1103
01:10:22,264 --> 01:10:26,310
18, 17, 16...

1104
01:10:27,186 --> 01:10:31,940
15, 14, 13...

1105
01:10:32,649 --> 01:10:34,318
12...

1106
01:10:34,359 --> 01:10:36,069
11...

1107
01:10:36,111 --> 01:10:40,240
10, 9, 8...

1108
01:10:40,282 --> 01:10:43,118
7, 6...

1109
01:10:44,495 --> 01:10:45,787
- What is that?
- What's happening?

1110
01:11:11,980 --> 01:11:14,399
- She's going for this bridge.
- No.

1111
01:11:15,609 --> 01:11:16,860
She's coming for Franklin.

1112
01:11:18,612 --> 01:11:20,781
- Oh, my God.
- Lock the building down!

1113
01:11:22,783 --> 01:11:25,369
Wait. Where's Johnny?

1114
01:11:55,941 --> 01:11:57,776
- Shalla-Bal.
- Shalla-Bal.

1115
01:11:57,818 --> 01:11:58,861
Shalla-Bal!

1116
01:12:28,807 --> 01:12:31,018
How do you know that name?

1117
01:12:31,059 --> 01:12:33,103
And how did you get these?

1118
01:12:36,273 --> 01:12:37,774
How?

1119
01:12:37,816 --> 01:12:39,651
He barely has a grasp
of the English language.

1120
01:12:39,693 --> 01:12:42,070
Twenty-three transmissions,

1121
01:12:42,112 --> 01:12:44,406
all in your language,

1122
01:12:44,448 --> 01:12:47,117
trace back
to the planet Zenn-La.

1123
01:12:48,118 --> 01:12:50,287
Your home.

1124
01:12:51,872 --> 01:12:56,001
They were looking for you,
to thank you.

1125
01:12:56,043 --> 01:12:59,087
Once I translated one phrase,

1126
01:12:59,129 --> 01:13:00,881
I pieced together
enough language

1127
01:13:00,923 --> 01:13:03,592
to understand
a part of your history.

1128
01:13:04,801 --> 01:13:08,680
You were some sort of
scientist or astronomer.

1129
01:13:10,098 --> 01:13:12,935
When Galactus came, you
offered to serve as his scout

1130
01:13:12,976 --> 01:13:14,436
if he'd spare your planet.

1131
01:13:15,896 --> 01:13:17,981
Was it to spare your family?

1132
01:13:40,212 --> 01:13:42,172
He turned you into this.

1133
01:13:46,176 --> 01:13:47,219
Shalla-Bal.

1134
01:13:48,512 --> 01:13:52,516
Those were messages from the
one planet Galactus spared.

1135
01:13:52,558 --> 01:13:53,976
Your planet.

1136
01:13:56,103 --> 01:13:58,355
These planets
weren't so lucky.

1137
01:14:01,358 --> 01:14:03,694
How many
do you remember, Shalla-Bal?

1138
01:14:03,735 --> 01:14:07,489
Proxima Delphi. Saigas.

1139
01:14:07,531 --> 01:14:08,991
Do you remember Polaris?

1140
01:14:11,160 --> 01:14:15,122
They begged for mercy.

1141
01:14:15,164 --> 01:14:18,625
You brought Galactus
to all of these planets.

1142
01:14:18,667 --> 01:14:21,753
And now
you're bringing him here,

1143
01:14:21,795 --> 01:14:24,882
to my home, to my family!

1144
01:14:42,774 --> 01:14:44,776
Just trying to save my world,
you know,

1145
01:14:46,320 --> 01:14:47,529
like you did.

1146
01:14:52,659 --> 01:14:54,828
So give up the child.

1147
01:14:54,870 --> 01:14:57,873
If he was older,
he would do it himself.

1148
01:14:59,333 --> 01:15:00,375
Like I did.

1149
01:15:01,168 --> 01:15:02,669
So take me.

1150
01:15:04,838 --> 01:15:06,465
Take me.

1151
01:15:06,507 --> 01:15:07,716
Not the boy.

1152
01:15:09,510 --> 01:15:12,054
Let me make the sacrifice.

1153
01:15:13,347 --> 01:15:15,182
It's not yours to make.

1154
01:15:15,891 --> 01:15:17,684
Then stay and help us.

1155
01:15:19,102 --> 01:15:20,437
There is no help.

1156
01:15:22,481 --> 01:15:25,400
Take the child
and leave this doomed place.

1157
01:15:26,777 --> 01:15:29,363
Maybe you'll live long enough
to forgive yourselves.

1158
01:15:39,164 --> 01:15:41,834
- Johnny, that was incredible.
- I mean, does it even matter?

1159
01:15:41,875 --> 01:15:43,085
You saved Franklin.

1160
01:15:43,752 --> 01:15:44,962
Yes, it matters.

1161
01:15:45,003 --> 01:15:46,129
Reed?

1162
01:15:47,714 --> 01:15:48,882
We're not leaving, are we?

1163
01:15:49,758 --> 01:15:51,426
No. No, we're not.

1164
01:15:54,680 --> 01:15:55,806
We're not leaving.

1165
01:16:02,813 --> 01:16:05,524
Um- Uh, yeah. Same here.

1166
01:16:05,566 --> 01:16:07,109
You gotta give us a second.
Um...

1167
01:16:07,151 --> 01:16:09,069
Yeah, this is Johnny Storm.
Can you hear me?

1168
01:16:09,111 --> 01:16:10,696
The line's too busy.

1169
01:16:10,737 --> 01:16:12,489
- I'm sorry, okay?
- This is London.

1170
01:16:12,531 --> 01:16:14,408
- This is London. Do you copy?
- Hold, London.

1171
01:16:14,449 --> 01:16:16,076
What's going on?

1172
01:16:17,911 --> 01:16:19,913
Hold, Paris.
Paris, hold.

1173
01:16:19,955 --> 01:16:21,456
The line's not very clear.

1174
01:16:21,498 --> 01:16:22,749
- Can you say that again?
- Hold the line.

1175
01:16:23,834 --> 01:16:25,335
Chicago, yes, we're onto it.

1176
01:16:25,377 --> 01:16:28,172
We're just, uh-
We're fixing the problem.

1177
01:16:32,009 --> 01:16:33,343
We're trying to get, uh...

1178
01:16:33,385 --> 01:16:34,887
We're trying
to get on top of this.

1179
01:16:34,928 --> 01:16:36,513
- Sydney, stand by.
- Yep. Got it.

1180
01:16:36,555 --> 01:16:38,724
- Tokyo, stand by.
- Hold. Hold.

1181
01:16:38,765 --> 01:16:40,392
We have to bring him here.

1182
01:16:40,434 --> 01:16:42,895
- We are aware.
- Yes, I understand.

1183
01:16:42,936 --> 01:16:45,063
- Can you stand by?
- We are aware.

1184
01:16:45,105 --> 01:16:47,983
- I'll update you.
- Yeah. Yeah.

1185
01:16:48,025 --> 01:16:50,527
We need to
bring Galactus here.

1186
01:16:50,569 --> 01:16:52,696
I will come back
to you. Hold.

1187
01:16:52,738 --> 01:16:53,947
- Call you back.
- Hold up.

1188
01:16:54,490 --> 01:16:56,033
Reed?

1189
01:16:56,074 --> 01:16:58,327
We need Galactus to come here?

1190
01:16:58,368 --> 01:17:00,871
I feel like we just spent a lot of time
trying to prevent that from happening.

1191
01:17:00,913 --> 01:17:02,915
Listen to me. We need to
get him away from his ship.

1192
01:17:02,956 --> 01:17:05,959
We need to bring him here,
to Times Square.

1193
01:17:06,001 --> 01:17:07,836
And then what?

1194
01:17:07,878 --> 01:17:10,631
And then, instead of moving
a planet away from one giant,

1195
01:17:10,672 --> 01:17:13,675
we move one giant
away from the planet.

1196
01:17:13,717 --> 01:17:17,304
If we route every power grid
on the Eastern Seaboard,

1197
01:17:17,346 --> 01:17:21,475
through our one last bridge,
charge back up,

1198
01:17:21,517 --> 01:17:25,145
we can keep
the portal open for...

1199
01:17:34,446 --> 01:17:35,572
Thirty-seven seconds.

1200
01:17:35,614 --> 01:17:38,408
Thirty... Not a lot of time

1201
01:17:38,450 --> 01:17:40,285
to throw a space god
off a planet.

1202
01:17:40,327 --> 01:17:42,538
- No, it is not.
- And where do we send him?

1203
01:17:42,579 --> 01:17:44,456
To the far edges
of the universe.

1204
01:17:44,498 --> 01:17:46,208
Without a ship,
he'll be stranded.

1205
01:17:46,250 --> 01:17:48,210
How are we supposed to
get Galactus to Times Square?

1206
01:17:48,252 --> 01:17:51,547
And how do we move one giant
through one large bridge?

1207
01:17:55,092 --> 01:17:57,010
I haven't figured
that part out yet.

1208
01:18:01,014 --> 01:18:02,141
You have.

1209
01:18:03,058 --> 01:18:04,643
Have what?

1210
01:18:04,685 --> 01:18:06,895
We have to use the only thing
Galactus wants.

1211
01:18:06,937 --> 01:18:08,689
No. I'll think of another way.

1212
01:18:08,730 --> 01:18:10,149
- What are you talking about?
- You can't.

1213
01:18:10,190 --> 01:18:11,400
You can't think
of another way.

1214
01:18:11,441 --> 01:18:13,068
- I will.
- There is only one way.

1215
01:18:13,110 --> 01:18:14,486
What are you talking about?

1216
01:18:16,780 --> 01:18:18,490
We have to use Franklin.

1217
01:18:21,326 --> 01:18:22,870
Yes.

1218
01:18:22,911 --> 01:18:24,079
You wanna use the boy?

1219
01:18:27,791 --> 01:18:29,668
You wanna use the boy as bait.

1220
01:18:29,710 --> 01:18:31,587
- No.
- That's your plan?

1221
01:18:31,628 --> 01:18:33,630
No, it's not my plan.
It's our plan.

1222
01:18:33,672 --> 01:18:35,215
It's the only plan.

1223
01:18:35,257 --> 01:18:36,925
It's not my plan.
I hate that plan.

1224
01:18:36,967 --> 01:18:38,886
- It's a bad plan. Stupid plan.
- Terrible idea.

1225
01:18:38,927 --> 01:18:42,264
Why don't I just burn through his ship?
That's another plan.

1226
01:18:42,306 --> 01:18:43,432
He's your kid
we're talking about.

1227
01:18:43,474 --> 01:18:44,600
Sue.

1228
01:18:44,641 --> 01:18:47,060
- I know.
- Sue. Sue.

1229
01:18:47,102 --> 01:18:48,937
Yes, I know. I know. I know!

1230
01:19:17,966 --> 01:19:21,386
I thought this was one of the most
beautiful things we'd ever built.

1231
01:19:23,847 --> 01:19:25,432
Feels terrifying now.

1232
01:19:27,100 --> 01:19:28,852
It can be beautiful again.

1233
01:19:30,395 --> 01:19:31,772
Everything can.

1234
01:19:40,697 --> 01:19:43,325
They've been gone a while.

1235
01:19:45,327 --> 01:19:46,370
Johnny.

1236
01:19:47,246 --> 01:19:48,455
Go check. See if they're back.

1237
01:19:48,497 --> 01:19:52,125
I'm in no rush to do that.

1238
01:19:52,167 --> 01:19:53,669
Well, I'm definitely not
gonna check.

1239
01:19:53,710 --> 01:19:55,337
I'm definitely
not going either.

1240
01:19:55,379 --> 01:19:56,797
Thank you
for going and checking.

1241
01:19:56,839 --> 01:19:58,423
You're welcome.
It's the least I could do

1242
01:19:58,465 --> 01:19:59,550
to say thank you for
going down to check first.

1243
01:19:59,591 --> 01:20:00,801
I'm definitely not going down.

1244
01:20:00,843 --> 01:20:02,636
- Chickenshits.
- Jesus.

1245
01:20:02,678 --> 01:20:04,221
Don't do that.

1246
01:20:04,263 --> 01:20:05,597
- I hate it when you do that.
- Don't do that.

1247
01:20:05,639 --> 01:20:08,142
Come on.
Let's run through the details.

1248
01:20:09,935 --> 01:20:11,728
I don't like
when she does that.

1249
01:20:11,770 --> 01:20:13,438
It's like...

1250
01:20:13,480 --> 01:20:15,774
It's unsettling when people
just appear like that.

1251
01:20:17,818 --> 01:20:20,195
Bombproof. Shockproof.

1252
01:20:21,155 --> 01:20:22,614
Radiation-proof.

1253
01:20:26,368 --> 01:20:28,745
Franklin will go here
when Galactus arrives.

1254
01:20:30,205 --> 01:20:33,500
Hey, do we know what direction
Galactus will be coming from?

1255
01:20:34,877 --> 01:20:36,503
Well, it could be
from anywhere.

1256
01:20:36,545 --> 01:20:39,756
But when he crosses
those lines, we trigger it.

1257
01:20:41,884 --> 01:20:44,428
We're in
the very center of the city.

1258
01:20:44,470 --> 01:20:48,515
We're surrounded by
miles of apartment buildings.

1259
01:20:48,557 --> 01:20:50,642
Any path he takes,
he's gonna be going through

1260
01:20:50,684 --> 01:20:52,978
thousands and thousands
of families.

1261
01:20:54,688 --> 01:20:56,440
I got an idea you'll hate.

1262
01:20:59,443 --> 01:21:02,196
Oh, my.

1263
01:21:02,237 --> 01:21:03,906
Very advanced.

1264
01:21:03,947 --> 01:21:08,160
So this must be
where the sausage is made.

1265
01:21:09,495 --> 01:21:12,039
I think I prefer just trying
to steal the sausage.

1266
01:21:12,080 --> 01:21:13,499
Please, don't touch.

1267
01:21:14,583 --> 01:21:15,459
Oh!

1268
01:21:16,126 --> 01:21:17,419
We'll fix that.

1269
01:21:17,461 --> 01:21:18,420
The...

1270
01:21:18,462 --> 01:21:19,755
Harvey.

1271
01:21:19,796 --> 01:21:22,508
Hello there, little robot man.

1272
01:21:22,549 --> 01:21:24,426
Could you dim the lights
for me, please?

1273
01:21:26,553 --> 01:21:29,473
Harvey, we wanted
to ask you something.

1274
01:21:29,515 --> 01:21:33,185
And whatever it is,
I would like him to ask me.

1275
01:21:33,227 --> 01:21:35,979
It's not-
It's not Reed or me asking.

1276
01:21:36,021 --> 01:21:37,689
It's the entire planet asking.

1277
01:21:37,731 --> 01:21:39,483
It wouldn't be the entire
planet now, would it?

1278
01:21:39,525 --> 01:21:40,859
Just the over part.

1279
01:21:40,901 --> 01:21:42,569
No, Mr. Elder.
We've met Galactus.

1280
01:21:42,611 --> 01:21:44,112
He'll eat
the under part first.

1281
01:21:44,154 --> 01:21:48,242
Well, regardless,
why don't you butter me up?

1282
01:21:51,411 --> 01:21:52,871
Spread it on.

1283
01:21:52,913 --> 01:21:54,873
- Okay, Mole Man.
- Mole Man?

1284
01:21:54,915 --> 01:21:56,416
You touch another piece
of my-

1285
01:21:56,458 --> 01:21:57,835
- Enough.
- Take the "mole" out of it.

1286
01:21:57,876 --> 01:21:59,253
- It's Mr. Elder to you.
- That is enough.

1287
01:21:59,294 --> 01:22:00,838
Give us a minute.
Just give us a minute.

1288
01:22:00,879 --> 01:22:03,215
Yes, that's it.

1289
01:22:03,257 --> 01:22:05,634
Johnny, don't be mad.
I didn't dress you.

1290
01:22:05,676 --> 01:22:07,469
Don't listen to him.
You're handsome.

1291
01:22:08,804 --> 01:22:09,972
Harvey.

1292
01:22:10,013 --> 01:22:11,890
I'm sorry, Sue. I'm...

1293
01:22:12,683 --> 01:22:14,184
End of days.

1294
01:22:14,226 --> 01:22:16,478
We all gotta learn
how to laugh.

1295
01:22:17,312 --> 01:22:19,815
So what do you need?

1296
01:22:19,857 --> 01:22:21,942
Evacuation orders
are in effect

1297
01:22:21,984 --> 01:22:23,402
in the Greater New York area.

1298
01:22:23,443 --> 01:22:25,154
